[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles Software Requirements Specification for HVPS Interface Board Bootloader
UID: DHF-HRC-0021
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: hvps-interface/bootloader

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this document is to provide Software Requirements Specifications for the Heracles HVPS
Interface Bootloader Firmware (FW).
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document describes all requirements of the Heracles HVPS Interface Bootloader FW.
The information in this document has been derived from the VoxelRay Heracles Product Requirements
Specification, as referenced in this document.

\*The term Software applies to both Software and Firmware systems.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
FW
  Firmware

HVPS
  High Voltage Power Supply

LED
  Light Emitting Diode

MCU
  Microcontroller Unit

PID
  Proportional Integral Derivative controller

PRS
  Product Requirements Specification

SDP
  Software Development Plan

SRS
  Software Requirements Specification

SW
  Software
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS Interface Bootloader firmware allows the system to be able to update the HVPS Interface
application firmware. The HVPS Interface Bootloader firmware runs on the MCU of the HVPS interface
board.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: References

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
EMS-WI-057-13: Generating Documents and Traceability Matrix Analysis in Ketryx WI

EMS-SOP-057: Software Design Control

DHF-HRC-0001, Rev. 2: Heracles Software Development Plan (SDP)

DHF-HRC-0002: VoxelRay Product Requirements Specification (PRS)
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Jump to Application on Valid CRC
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall jump to execution of the HVPS interface application
if and only if the existing application code at startup is valid. The application code is valid if the
programmed CRC value matches the application firmware loaded in flash memory.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Write Flash Memory Page
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to write a specified flash memory page with
provided data from the PC.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-3
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Erase Flash Memory
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to erase a predetermined area of flash
memory, corresponding to the application firmware programming area.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-4
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: PC Communication Ping Response
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to respond to a ping command from the PC,
indicating that the system is in bootloader mode.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
